{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.HardWallProjection","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HardWallProjection","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.BigOperators.Group.Finset","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Ring.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Ring.Finset","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Positivity"],"declarations":4,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HardWallProjection.linear_sub_excess_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HardWallProjection.linear_sub_excess_le","kind":"theorem","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HardWallProjection.lean#L92-L116","doc":"**The scalar trade-off.** A loss `c·y` linear in the distance to the reference, against an\nenergy `(L/2)·max(0, y² − y₀²)`, is bounded by `c·y₀ + c²/(2L)` uniformly in `y ≥ 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HardWallProjection.shiftDiff_le_of_reference","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HardWallProjection.shiftDiff_le_of_reference","kind":"theorem","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HardWallProjection.lean#L79-L90","doc":"Linearity of `Δ_k`: `Δ_k(t) = Δ_k(p) + Δ_k(t − p)`. Combined with\n`shiftDiff_nonpos_of_monotone`, `Δ_k(t) ≤ Δ_k(t − p)`, which Cauchy–Schwarz bounds by\n`√(2 min(k, l−k))·‖t − p‖`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HardWallProjection.shiftDiff_nonpos_of_monotone","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HardWallProjection.shiftDiff_nonpos_of_monotone","kind":"theorem","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HardWallProjection.lean#L70-L77","doc":"The neighbour-order-`k` difference `Δ_k(v) = Σ_{i < m} (v i − v (i+k))` of a monotone sequence\nis non-positive: the water-filling reference never widens a mean `k`-th neighbour distance. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HardWallProjection.waterfill_pythagoras","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HardWallProjection.waterfill_pythagoras","kind":"theorem","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HardWallProjection.lean#L44-L68","doc":"**Water-filling Pythagoras.** If `p i = max τ (w i)` on `s`, `t` lies above the wall `w`, and\n`t`, `p` have the same sum, then `Σ p² + Σ (t − p)² ≤ Σ t²`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}